{"html":"<p>The most visible Rust success story is the one you use every day: the tools in\nyour terminal got faster, and most of them got faster by being rewritten in Rust.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-domain-demands\">What the domain demands</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Requirement</th>\n<th>Consequence</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Sub-50 ms startup</td>\n<td>A tool you run 500 times a day must not think</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No runtime to install</td>\n<td>A single static binary — download, run, done</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Correct on weird input</td>\n<td>UTF-8, CRLF, symlinks, 4 GB files, no trailing newline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Composable</td>\n<td>stdin/stdout, exit codes, <code>NO_COLOR</code>, <code>--json</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cross-platform</td>\n<td>The same binary on macOS, Linux, Windows, ARM</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Startup time is the constraint that kills interpreted tools. A 300 ms JVM start\nis fine for a server and fatal for a linter.</p>\n<h2 id=\"who-runs-it\">Who runs it</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tool</th>\n<th>Replaced</th>\n<th>The number</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>ripgrep</strong></td>\n<td><code>grep -r</code>, <code>ag</code></td>\n<td>often 2–10× faster, respects <code>.gitignore</code> by default</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>fd</strong></td>\n<td><code>find</code></td>\n<td>simpler syntax, parallel traversal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>bat</strong></td>\n<td><code>cat</code></td>\n<td>syntax highlighting with a <code>cat</code>-compatible interface</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>uv</strong></td>\n<td><code>pip</code> + <code>virtualenv</code></td>\n<td>Astral's package manager; installs that took a minute finish in a second</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Deno</strong></td>\n<td>Node.js</td>\n<td>Rust host embedding V8, with a capability-secure stdlib</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>swc</strong></td>\n<td>Babel</td>\n<td>a JS/TS compiler in Rust, used by Next.js</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Turbopack</strong></td>\n<td>webpack</td>\n<td>Vercel's incremental bundler</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Biome</strong></td>\n<td>ESLint + Prettier</td>\n<td>one Rust binary doing lint and format</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>zoxide, starship, hyperfine, delta</strong></td>\n<td>assorted shell tools</td>\n<td>startup budgets measured in single-digit milliseconds</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Notice the pattern: <strong>a better interface was not enough; the tools had to be\nfaster.</strong> ripgrep did not win by adding features to grep — it won by being\nresponsive on a monorepo.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-shape-of-the-code\">The shape of the code</h2>\n<p>The core of a fast file walker, using the same crate ripgrep uses:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> ignore</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">WalkBuilder</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> std</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">sync</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">atomic</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dar